  "static_review": {
    "input": "Three strings preserve spelling/case/Unicode/whitespace. New adapter rejects invalid UTF-8, unsafe single basename and >128KiB request before HostCaller. These are explicitly documented adapter limits, not original Python validation. Directory/ID/hash grant no authority.",
    "prepare": "Required skipped and temporary pointers distinguish absent/null. Skip forbids transfer fields and rebuilt=true; successful bytes require five semantic fields with valid opaque token, total 0..16MiB and lowercase SHA256. Skipped has nil Content; successful zero bytes are nonnil.",
    "read": "Sequential offsets and exact same token; base64-only data, exactly min(1MiB,remaining), complete byte count and full SHA256 before result. At most 16 reads for a valid 16MiB object. No folder/files/path/TorrentInfo are invented.",
    "cleanup": "Valid syntactic prepare handle registers same-capability/same-HostCaller deferred release before strict prepare validation. Malformed allocated result/read/digest/cancel failures still attempt release with one-second cancellation-detached context. Release error/false/malformed receipt prevents returning complete bytes; an earlier error is retained and partial result cleared.",
    "authority_boundary": "Detached cleanup does not itself authorize anything; host must revalidate the same invocation and final scope close must reclaim allocations. That host behavior is not tested by recording callbacks. Release is not disk deletion; Temporary=false does not certify no partially written disk material.",
    "decoder_precision": "Reuses unchanged torrentMaterialDecode: UTF-8/size/null/unknown-field/trailing-value guards and standard encoding/json struct member handling. No additional canonical member-case or duplicate-key rejection is introduced or claimed by this finite review.",
    "no_product_IO": "New SDK imports no os/network/process APIs and never reads or writes backup/temp files. App root/type/authority/error-latch and deterministic hash disk reuse remain outside this SDK gate."
  },
